.TH CVECTOR_DESTROY 3 "2026-09-28" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cvector_destroy \- destroy a vector and set pointer to NULL
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cvector.h>

cvector_destroy(v)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Frees every resource of the vector, the data buffer included, and then
sets the vector pointer to NULL.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
v    Vector to destroy, which must be a modifiable lvalue such as a
     variable or an element of an array. The macro evaluates it exactly
     once and sets it to NULL
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Safe to call with a NULL pointer (a no-op)
Does not free the elements one by one, so the caller must first free
any heap buffers that the elements point to, when this is necessary
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cvector_create (3)
